CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process; and
j. the right to assistance.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
Protection of women and children from acts of violence is conducted based on the principles of:
a. humanity;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. protection;
d. best interests of women and children; and
e. non-discrimination.

Article 3
The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence are to:
a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect, provide a sense of security for women and children; d. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

